  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be two relations defined on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nHKSV",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is an equivalence relation but not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9uYjh",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is an equivalence relation but not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jYpmm",
      "text": "both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are equivalence relations",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "X9OLV",
      "text": "neither <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;nor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is an equivalence relation",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>For reflexive&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;which is true,</p><p>For symmetric</p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;which is true,</p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;but&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is not true</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;not transitive relation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is not equivalence</p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;it does not implies&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is not equivalence relation</p><p>So, neither <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;nor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is an equivalence relation</p></blockquote>",
